  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On August 20, the US Treasury Department's Office of Foreign Assets Control added 17 individuals and eight entities to the Hezbollah-linked designation list — the most extensive single Hezbollah-related OFAC action since the MOU period opened in June 2026 (CNN, August 20). The designations target financial conduits in Lebanon, Iraq, and the UAE. State Department spokespersons declined questions about concurrent diplomatic contacts in a briefing cited by CNN, and no mediator communiqué accompanied the announcement. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move</p>

      <p>Iran parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, speaking in Tehran on August 22, described receiving "messages from neighboring nations about shaping new security commitments and economic cooperation in the region" and characterized the goal as a "homegrown, independent" regional security order (Al Jazeera live updates, August 22). No neighboring state government published a joint communiqué, and no Iranian MFA statement mentioned a resumption of mediated US-Iran engagement in the same 48-hour window. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>

      <p>Commercial maritime transit through the Strait of Hormuz remained at approximately 10 to 12 vessels per day through the week of August 17-23, per Al Jazeera and CNN, against a pre-conflict baseline of approximately 130 per day. Dark-fleet activity — vessels running with AIS transponders disabled — surpassed AIS-visible commercial traffic in volume for the first time, Lloyd's List Intelligence reported in its August 19 Hormuz Brief. CNN (August 21) confirmed US gasoline prices ran nearly one dollar above year-ago levels, with no White House comment on a reopening timeline. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>

      <p>Israeli forces continued operations in southern Lebanon through August 22, with the Board of Peace urging restraint after Kushner met with PM Netanyahu to request that strikes be limited to imminent threats (Times of Israel, August 19). Hezbollah threatened an "appropriate response" to Israeli strikes that killed 11 in southern Lebanon on August 15 — including Badr unit commander Abu Hassan Alaa — but had not executed any publicly-claimed retaliatory strike as of the August 23 reporting cutoff, eight days after the threat. → supports <span class="cite">F1</span> without move, supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move</p>

      <p>The Trump administration stated on August 22 that Iran "was not ready for the right deal" and that Washington was "observing what happens" — the most recent named-official characterization of US-Iran relations, citing no upcoming meeting or mediator deployment (Al Jazeera live updates, August 22). Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian attended a ceremony at Imam Khomeini's burial site in Tehran on August 23 (Tehran Times) — a routine annual event that produced no foreign-policy statement. IRGC General Staff, via Tasnim (August 23), issued warnings that weapons would be "completely different from the past in every respect" if hostilities resume. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP (computed summary) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:43%;">Escalation 43%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-status" style="width:43%;">Protracted 43%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:14%;">De-esc 14%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (43%):</strong> F4 YES (p=0.38) or F1 YES (p=0.22) — an IRGC/Hezbollah qualifying strike or Hezbollah's Aug 15 retaliation executing — would draw Israeli response and further close the already-narrow diplomatic window; combined probability via independence assumption: ~1−(0.62×0.78)=0.52, discounted to 43% for potential containment.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (43%):</strong> F4 NO and F1 NO and F2 NO and F3 below threshold — no qualifying strike, talks frozen, Hormuz locked near 10/day — defines a static-pressure equilibrium that remains the base case through mid-September.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (14%):</strong> F2 YES (p=0.12) is the primary pathway; resumption of a convened US-Iran session before September 4 is the necessary but not sufficient condition; without an active mediator deployment as of August 23, this path is materially constrained.</p>
    </div>
